      "text": "(B.2)"
    },
    "preceding_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 93326,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 4634,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 1799,
        "paragraph_id": "2D55A9BC",
        "text": "Where A is the wave energy or wave action, cg is the group velocity, cΘ the refraction speed in theta-space and SINK refers to effects of wave breaking, vegetation and bottom friction. Again, the advection terms are the only ones affected by the curvilinear scheme so we will discuss their treatment in detail. The control volume is the same as for the mass balance. In (B.1) the procedure to compute the wave energy fluxes across the cell boundaries is outlined. All variables should also have an index itheta referring to the directional grid, but for brevity these are omitted here."
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 93441,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 4636,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 1801,
        "paragraph_id": "7D038DF6",
        "text": "The component of the group velocity normal to the cell boundary, at the cell boundary, is interpolated from the two adjacent cell center points. Depending on the direction of this component, the wave energy at the cell boundary is computed using linear extrapolation based on the two upwind points, taking into account their grid distances. This second order upwind discretization preserves the propagation of wave groups with little numerical diffusion."
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 93539,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 4640,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 1805,
        "paragraph_id": "21B4B861",
        "text": "The other three fluxes are computed in a similar way; for brevity we will not present all formulations."
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 93551,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 4642,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 1807,
        "paragraph_id": "014E156E",
        "text": "The time integration is explicit and the same as in the original implementation. The advection in u- and v-direction is computed simply by adding the four fluxes and dividing by the cell area. This procedure guarantees conservation of wave energy."
      }
    ],
    "table_cell": null,
    "text_method": "Saved display-field substitution plus w:t; equation objects are not transcribed."
  },
